---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lessons = [
  {
    number: 41,
    title: "Smooth Scrolling Text",
    description: "Message scrolls smoothly with hardware registers",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 42,
    title: "Multi-Sprite Patterns",
    description: "Formation of 8 sprites moving together",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 43,
    title: "Custom Character Set",
    description: "Define custom characters for game graphics",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 44,
    title: "Advanced Sound",
    description: "Sound effects with SID envelope & waveform",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 45,
    title: "Screen Transitions",
    description: "Fade in/out and wipe effects",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 46,
    title: "Save/Load to Disk",
    description: "Save game state and load it back",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 47,
    title: "Raster Timing Basics",
    description: "Colour bar splits screen with raster",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 48,
    title: "BASIC Performance Tips",
    description: "Compare slow vs fast techniques",
    status: "available"
  }
];
---

<Layout title="Week 6: Advanced Techniques - Commodore 64">
  <style>
    .course-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #8b5cf6 0%, #7c3aed 100%);
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .course-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    }

    .course-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .course-description {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      opacity: 0.95;
    }

    .course-stats {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .stat-item {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .stat-value {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .stat-label {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      opacity: 0.9;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .content-container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .intro-section {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #8b5cf6;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-8);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .intro-section h2 {
      color: #8b5cf6;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .intro-section p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .intro-section ul {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      padding-left: var(--space-6);
    }

    .intro-section li {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    .lessons-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .lesson-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      align-items: center;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .lesson-card:hover {
      border-color: #8b5cf6;
      transform: translateX(4px);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.1);
    }

    .lesson-number {
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #8b5cf6 0%, #7c3aed 100%);
      color: white;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .lesson-content {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .lesson-title {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .lesson-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .lesson-status {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
      border-radius: 9999px;
      background: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.1);
      color: #8b5cf6;
    }

    .start-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #8b5cf6 0%, #7c3aed 100%);
      color: white;
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .start-button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.3);
    }

    .wow-box {
      background: var(--color-bg);
      border-left: 4px solid #8b5cf6;
      padding: var(--space-4);
      margin: var(--space-6) 0;
      border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
    }

    .wow-box strong {
      color: #8b5cf6;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .lesson-card {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .lesson-number {
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      .lesson-status {
        justify-self: center;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Course Hero -->
  <section class="course-hero">
    <h1 class="course-title">WEEK 6: ADVANCED TECHNIQUES</h1>
    <p class="course-subtitle">Hardware Tricks & Optimization</p>

    <p class="course-description">
      You can build games. Now learn the tricks that make them spectacular. Week 6 teaches advanced C64 techniques—hardware scrolling, multi-sprite formations, custom graphics, advanced sound, screen effects, disk saves, raster timing, and performance optimization. These are the secrets behind professional C64 titles.
    </p>

    <div class="course-stats">
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">8</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Advanced Lessons</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">Pro</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Level Tricks</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">100%</div>
        <div class="stat-label">BASIC Power</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Course Introduction -->
  <div class="content-container">
    <section class="intro-section">
      <h2>What You'll Learn This Week</h2>

      <p>
        Week 6 reveals the advanced techniques that separate amateur games from professional titles. By the end of these 8 lessons, you'll know the tricks commercial developers used:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Smooth scrolling text</strong> with hardware scroll registers for marquee effects</li>
        <li><strong>Multi-sprite patterns</strong> coordinating all 8 sprites with formation movement</li>
        <li><strong>Custom character sets</strong> redefining graphics for unique game visuals</li>
        <li><strong>Advanced SID sound</strong> with envelope, waveform, and filter for professional audio</li>
        <li><strong>Screen transitions</strong> fade in/out, wipe effects for scene changes</li>
        <li><strong>Disk save/load</strong> persisting game state across sessions</li>
        <li><strong>Raster timing</strong> colour bar splits and mid-screen effects</li>
        <li><strong>Performance optimization</strong> comparing slow vs fast BASIC techniques</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="wow-box">
        <strong>Week 6 Goal:</strong> By Lesson 48, you'll know the hardware tricks that define C64 classics. Smooth scrolling like Defender, multi-sprite formations like Uridium, custom graphics like Boulder Dash, and performance techniques that squeeze every bit of speed from BASIC.
      </div>

      <p>
        <strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Complete Weeks 1-5 first! These advanced techniques build on solid fundamentals and assume you're comfortable with sprites, sound, and game mechanics.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Learning approach:</strong> Each lesson focuses on ONE advanced trick. See the simple version, then the WOW moment showing how pros used it. These techniques appear in every classic C64 game you've played—now you'll know how they work.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Lessons List -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Lessons</h2>

      <div class="lessons-grid">
        {lessons.map(lesson => (
          <a href={`/commodore-64/basic/week-6/lesson-${String(lesson.number).padStart(2, '0')}`}
             class="lesson-card">
            <div class="lesson-number">{lesson.number}</div>
            <div class="lesson-content">
              <h3 class="lesson-title">{lesson.title}</h3>
              <p class="lesson-description">{lesson.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-status">Start →</div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Call to Action -->
    <section style="text-align: center; margin: var(--space-16) 0;">
      <h2 class="section-title">Ready for Advanced Techniques?</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); max-width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        Week 6 unlocks the C64's full potential. Learn the hardware tricks and optimization techniques that professional developers used to create the games you love. This is where BASIC becomes powerful.
      </p>
      <a href="/commodore-64/basic/week-6/lesson-41" class="start-button">
        Start Lesson 41: Smooth Scrolling
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
